presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_9"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to spare", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give something, such as time, money to someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally asked Peter to spare some time for a coffee break.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about families.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "divorce", "type": "name"}, {"content": "when a couple decides to end their marriage and live separately", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally found out that her aunt and uncle are getting a divorce.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "extended family", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a family that includes parents, children and other relatives ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally is very close to her extended family.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "nuclear family", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a family that includes only the father, mother, and children", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Peter said his family will always be a nuclear family.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "single parent", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an unmarried person who has a child or children", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally doesn't want to be a single parent.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to end up ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to reach or come to a place or situation that was not expected", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She did not want to end up raising a child by herself.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Talking About the Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use both <span class=\"italic\">going to </span> and <span class=\"italic\">will</span> to talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>.<br><br>When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">going to</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Situation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sally says to Peter on the phone: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">\u201cI'll see you at the espresso bar in 5 minutes.\u201d</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sally has just agreed on a plan with Peter.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"going to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Two minutes later, Sally tells Vanessa on the phone:  <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> \u201cI'm going to have coffee with Peter.\u201d</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sally tells Vanessa the coffee plan has been been made. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "My aunt and uncle are going to get a divorce.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will be rich and famous, like my grandfather.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "What have you done? ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use Wh- questions in <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> to ask about the state of a person from a specific time or epoch in the past until the present. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Form: </span><br><span class=\"strong\">Wh</span> + auxiliary + subject + verb in past participle + complement? <br> <span class=\"strong\">What</span> <br> <span class=\"strong\">Where</span> <br> <span class=\"strong\">When</span> + have (I/you/they/we)<br> <span class=\"strong\">Why</span> + <span class=\"strong\">has</span> (he/she)<br> <span class=\"strong\">How long</span><br> <span class=\"strong\">How</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "How long <span class=\"strong\">have</span>  they <span class=\"strong\">been</span>  married? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How <span class=\"strong\">have</span>  the kids <span class=\"strong\">been</span>? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Where <span class=\"strong\">have</span>  you <span class=\"strong\">had</span> the coffee break this week?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What <span class=\"strong\">has</span>  she <span class=\"strong\">read</span>  lately?", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Choose one Latin country, one European country, and  one Asian country to research.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find out what the average family size in a home is in each country.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Are extended family included?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Fill the information into the following chart.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Country\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Average family size\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Extended family in home: (Y / N)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I research types of families in other cultures.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I determine average family sizes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I organize my research information into a table.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I communicate the information to my partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn6le10ob02re2img07.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn6le10ob02re2img07.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Hello, Peter speaking.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Hey, it's Sally. What's up?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Well, I'm working. How are you?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'm shopping in the area. Can you spare time for a quick coffee break?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Well, I've stared at the computer screen long enough. Let's go.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Awesome! I'll see you at the espresso bar in 5 minutes?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Sounds great!"}, {"image": "engenn6le10ob02re2img08.jpg", "time": "22000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: So, I just found out that my aunt and uncle are going to get a divorce.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Oh, your Aunt Katie and Uncle Nick? That's unfortunate. You must feel terrible.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I do because I'm so close to my extended family.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I don't believe it either. How long have they been married?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: They've been married for almost 35 years.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Wow. That's pretty impressive. How are their kids dealing with it?"}, {"image": "engenn6le10ob02re2img09.jpg", "time": "47500", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Not well, but they've all started their own families.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Well, I am certainly going to keep my future family a nuclear family.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Yeah, I will NOT end up being a single parent.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Or do what John and Sandra are planning: form a childless family."}], "audiosrc": "en